the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    the calculation date is *a date*; scenario element.
    the youth exemption lower age years is *a number*.
    the youth exemption upper age years is *a number*.
    the youth work requirement exemption of *a person* applies.
    *a person* is person otherwise required to comply with paragraph 1 requirements; scenario element.
    the person age years of *a person* is *a number*; scenario element.
    *a person* is snap household head; scenario element.
    *a person* is attending school at least half time; scenario element.
    *a person* is enrolled in employment training program at least half time; scenario element.

the knowledge base us_statutes_7_2015_d_2_f includes:


% 7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(2)(F) — us:statutes/7/2015/d/2/F
the text of "7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(2)(F)" is at "sources/us/statutes/7/2015/d/2/F.yaml".

rule youth_exemption_lower_age_years with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(2)(F)":
the youth exemption lower age years is 16 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D.

rule youth_exemption_upper_age_years with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(2)(F)":
the youth exemption upper age years is 18 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D.

rule youth_work_requirement_exemption_applies_1 with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(2)(F)":
the youth work requirement exemption of a person applies if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the person is person otherwise required to comply with paragraph 1 requirements
    and the person age years of the person is a number N
    and the youth exemption lower age years is a number M
    and N >= M
    and the person age years of the person is a number K
    and the youth exemption upper age years is a number P
    and K < P
    and it is not the case that the person is snap household head.

rule youth_work_requirement_exemption_applies_2 with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(2)(F)":
the youth work requirement exemption of a person applies if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the person is person otherwise required to comply with paragraph 1 requirements
    and the person age years of the person is a number N
    and the youth exemption lower age years is a number M
    and N >= M
    and the person age years of the person is a number K
    and the youth exemption upper age years is a number P
    and K < P
    and the person is attending school at least half time.

rule youth_work_requirement_exemption_applies_3 with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(2)(F)":
the youth work requirement exemption of a person applies if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the person is person otherwise required to comply with paragraph 1 requirements
    and the person age years of the person is a number N
    and the youth exemption lower age years is a number M
    and N >= M
    and the person age years of the person is a number K
    and the youth exemption upper age years is a number P
    and K < P
    and the person is enrolled in employment training program at least half time.

scenario youth_between_sixteen_and_eighteen_not_head_of_household_exempt is, as stated in "sources/us/statutes/7/2015/d/2/F.test.yaml" at case 1:
    person_1 is a person.
    the calculation date is 2026-01-01.
    the person age years of person_1 is 16.
    person_1 is person otherwise required to comply with paragraph 1 requirements.
    q_youth_work_requirement_exemption_applies expects answers ["the youth work requirement exemption of person_1 applies"].

